Author: ctymoszek <31750745+ctymoszek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 13:57:06 2026 -0400

    Add AI usage policy (#585)
    
    AI-generated code is allowed, and so is AI-drafted prose. What is not allowed is submitting either one without the human contributor understanding it. You must be able to explain the code you submit, you must disclose how you used AI, and you must read and approve any prose you submit. Agents may not autonomously create PRs or other reviewer-facing text without a human in the loop.
    
    Do not make reviewers read prose that you, the human, did not bother to read.
    
    The policy itself has been added to CONTRIBUTING.md, addressed to human contributors, including possible penalties if it is not followed. AGENTS.md is intended to help agents produce a submission with a better chance of being accepted. It contains the same rules, plus helpful local conventions and CI mechanics such as where CI's swift-format pin lives, the DocC check, and the fact that `swift test` does not work here. CLAUDE.md is a symlink to it. The pull request template asks the author to confirm they read the description and that it matches the code, and adds an AI usage disclosure that all submitters are expected to fill in. The issue templates now include the same acknowledgment.

