commit 476a4723b266dfa5152194a870f069058be6c8be
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 20:26:20 2026 +0400

    Replace MLXRandom.seed with task-local withRandomState in tests (#583)
    
    MLXRandom.seed resets MLXRandom.globalState, a process-wide singleton.
    Swift Testing runs tests in parallel, so tests seeding and consuming the
    global stream interleave their key splits: one test's seed call resets
    another test's stream mid-consumption, making seeded tests neither
    isolated nor reproducible.
    
    Every seeded test now scopes its randomness with
    withRandomState(MLXRandom.RandomState(seed:)), which binds a @TaskLocal
    random state that resolve(key:) prefers over the global state - the
    pattern Gemma4UnifiedTests and EvalTests already use. Each test owns a
    private, deterministic stream regardless of what runs concurrently.
    
    Also pins the previously unseeded tiny-model factories (Qwen3-VL,
    Qwen3.5, GLM-OCR, Nanbeige) under a task-local state so their
    tolerance-based equivalence assertions are reproducible when they fail,
    and drops the now-redundant .serialized trait from RoPEApplicationTests.
    
    Fixes #577

