commit 6745899c2d6fd2c2325055005f1d463237d44153
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 01:33:54 2026 +0400

    Add variance-normalized KV cache (#329)
    
    * Add variance-normalized KV cache
    
    Integrate a KVarN-inspired variance-normalized KV cache into the typed
    KVCacheConfiguration / KVCachePlan system introduced on main.
    
    - Hadamard rotation, dual-axis log-domain variance normalization, and
      asymmetric K/V quantization for completed tiles
    - Cache-native attention via KVCacheAttentionProtocol with stacked
      multi-tile quantized matmul for score and value projection
    - Typed strategy VarianceNormalizedKVCacheConfiguration plus legacy
      schemes (varn / varn4v2 / varn4v2t32, ...)
    - Dynamic conversion through applyKVCacheConfiguration; prompt-cache
      serialization for VarianceNormalizedKVCache
    - Unit, attention parity, memory, and quality-gate coverage
    
    Memory-bound long-context use case; slower than the default cache on the
    decode path by design.
    
    Reference: https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.03458

