    element of a frame's chunk shared the same base. For t > 1 the boundaries stopped
    short of the patch buffer, leaving the tail rows outside every attendable block.
    
    Extracted the computation to visionCuSeqlens(_:) so temporal grids can be covered
    directly: the mask bias is a finite -10000 rather than -inf, so a row outside every
    block attends uniformly instead of producing NaN, and only the boundaries themselves
    make the failure observable.

diff --git a/Libraries/MLXVLM/Models/Qwen25VL.swift b/Libraries/MLXVLM/Models/Qwen25VL.swift
