commit 2af378b3557384f6c6ce936fab8e9748a1e8d61a
Author: Cassie Spiral <166543307+angelsbrood@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 11 10:13:14 2026 -0700

    Speculate past the sliding window in MTP (#516)
    
    Add speculative-decoding support for `RotatingKVCache` via staged, transactional rounds.
    
    - `logicalView(tail:)`: read-only chronological view of a rotating cache, without mutating state; contract corrected to account for pinned prefixes.
    - `roundIsOpen` guard: rejects cache mutation/snapshot while a speculative round is mid-flight.
    - `beginRound`/commit on `KVCacheStorage`: makes speculative writes transactional per-leaf (`KVCacheRoundStrategy`), so rotating caches no longer need post-hoc trimming (which breaks once a ring has wrapped).
    - Committed rounds can be rewound exactly (`rewindLastRound`), resolved by cache slot rather than captured object, so dynamic compression or mixed sliding-window topologies can't rewind into the wrong leaf.
    - MTP drafting now works past the sliding window: rounds replace the old `trimPromptCache` rewind, so the drafter no longer stands down once context exceeds the window (fixes #474 for Gemma-style short windows).
    - Shared K/V snapshots are refused unless tagged with their source cache entries (`mtpSharedKVSourceIndicesKey`, now public), preventing unclamped attention over rejected drafts; all prefill/prime paths route through the same fallback.
    
    Net effect: speculative decoding remains correct and enabled across sliding-window boundaries that previously forced a silent fallback to unstaged decoding.

