commit 4b0b41631337e28da84c194fac7e2620dfa0f1b1
Author: Kirill Klimuk <kklimuk@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 10 14:04:54 2026 -0400

    Prompt cache: persist model state, wire Qwen3-VL and GLM-OCR restoration, and fail closed (#475)
    
    Persist model continuation state through prompt caches, fixing Qwen vision cache restoration and letting continuation state ride through speculative decoding.
    
    - Restore continuation state with prompt caches; fail closed when required state is missing.
    - Drop `requiresContinuationState`: it's a position anchor (`ropeDeltas`), not an accumulator, so it survives rejection/rollback and doesn't block speculation. Thread `state:` through the cache-taking `generate` helpers so restored snapshots keep their anchor.
    - Add batch guards, `components:` forwarding, and a speculation-restart fix for a warm main cache with no draft cache.
    - Adopt `PrefillParameters`/`forEachChunk` in Qwen3-VL, GLM-OCR, and Qwen3.5 for windowed continuation, replacing the deprecated `prepare` shim.
    - Document fragment continuation on the `promptCache:` initializers; narrow the note for models with unmasked/joint vision encoders (Qwen2-VL).
    - Cleanup: share the continuation anchor logic (`QwenVL.continuationAnchor`/`.continuationResumeState`) and chunk-forward helper across models; trim duplicated comments; minor perf fixes (hoist loop-invariant scatter indices, drop redundant GPU syncs).
    - Tests: shared `ContinuationAssertions` across model suites; new coverage for warm batched continuation, speculation restart, and progress reporting.
    
    Reported by @NivDvir (#475)

